# Phase 7 Implementation Design (Revision 9): Error Handling, Resilience & Concurrency Control

## 1) Phase extraction from `docs/SPECIFICATION.md`

### Goal
Harden reconciliation for production with retry logic, rate limiting, partial-failure convergence, and graceful degradation.

### Step-by-step actions (spec)
1. Implement retry wrapper in `internal/azure/retry.go` (exponential backoff + jitter, default max retries 3, respect `Retry-After` for 429).
2. Implement per-subscription rate limiter in `internal/azure/ratelimit.go` (default 10 RPS via `golang.org/x/time/rate`).
3. Implement reconcile error handling in `internal/controller/errors.go` (retriable vs non-retriable classification + requeue strategy).
4. Wire retry + rate limiting into ARM execution path.
5. Handle partial failures so successes persist, failures are reported in status, and reconcile requeues for convergence.

### Deliverables for this phase
1. ARM call loop uses `RetryPolicy`/`DecideRetry`, including `Retry-After` delays.
2. Per-subscription throttling applies before each ARM attempt.
3. Requeue decisions use `DecideRequeueFromActionSummary` / `DecideRequeueFromSystemError`.
4. System/pre-action failures and action failures are consistently surfaced to `PodASGMapping.status` when status is enabled.
5. Acceptance tests T7.1-T7.7 are covered with explicit implementation-path assertions.

### Type definitions in-scope
- `azure.RetryPolicy`, `azure.RetryDecision`, `azure.RetryContext`
- `azure.SubscriptionRateLimiter`
- `controller.ActionFailureSummary`, `controller.RequeuePolicy`
- `azure.ARMStatusError` (`StatusCode`, `ARMCode`, `RetryAfter`, `Operation`, `RequestURL`)

### TDD acceptance tests from spec
| ID | Scenario | Required assertion |
|---|---|---|
| T7.1 | ARM returns 429 | Retry waits according to `Retry-After` |
| T7.2 | ARM returns 500 three times then succeeds | Success on 4th attempt |
| T7.3 | ARM returns 500 four times | Retry exhausted and failure reported in status |
| T7.4 | ARM returns 403 | No retry and failure reported immediately in status |
| T7.5 | 3 of 5 actions fail | 2 succeed and persist, 3 reported, reconcile requeued |
| T7.6 | Rate limiter throttles burst of 20 calls | Calls spread over time, none dropped |
| T7.7 | ETag conflict during retry loop | Re-GET + recompute succeeds |

